module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Divisors.Meromorphic.DenominatorsInclusion
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Presheaf.ChangeOfRingsAdjunction
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Meromorphic.TotalQuotientSheafSections
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Meromorphic.NonZeroDivisorNowhereDense
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.InvertibleTrivialization.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.InvertibleClasses.Basic

/-!
# A meromorphic section of an invertible sheaf has a local nonzerodivisor denominator

Let `X` be a scheme, `L` an invertible sheaf of `𝒪_X`-modules and `s` a meromorphic section of
`L`. The proof of [Stacks, Tag 02P0](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02P0) begins by
shrinking `X` until `L` is trivial and `s = a/b` with `b` a nonzerodivisor; every later
assertion of the tag — quasi-coherence of the ideal `I` of denominators, and the nowhere dense
closed supports of the two cokernels — is read off from that normal form. This file supplies
exactly that step: around every point there is an **affine** open `V` and a nonzerodivisor
`b ∈ Γ(X, V)` which is a denominator of `s` on `V`, that is, `b · s` is the image of a section
of `L` over `V`. In the language of the tag, `b ∈ I(V)`, so `(b) ⊆ I` on `V`.

The statement is local on purpose. `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.totalQuotientSheaf` is the
*sheafification* of `U ↦ S(U)⁻¹𝒪_X(U)`, so a meromorphic section is only locally a fraction and
the corresponding global statement is false;
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Meromorphic/TotalQuotientSheafSections.lean` records the same
phenomenon for `K_X` itself.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.meromorphicTensorPresheaf`: the presheaf `K_X ⊗_{𝒪_X} L` whose
  sheafification is `K_X(L)`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.toSheafifyMeromorphicTensor`: the canonical map from that presheaf to
  `K_X(L)`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.oneTmulMeromorphicSectionSheaf`: the map `t ↦ 1 ⊗ t` from `L` to `K_X(L)`.
  It agrees on sections with `AlgebraicGeometry.toMeromorphicSectionSheafAsModule`, by
  `AlgebraicGeometry.oneTmulMeromorphicSectionSheaf_app_apply`.
* `Stacks.Meromorphic.sheafifyChangeOfRings`, `Stacks.Meromorphic.toSheafifyChangeOfRings`: the
  same two objects for an arbitrary morphism of sheaves of commutative rings on a site.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_isAffineOpen_nhds_toMeromorphicSectionSheafAsModule_eq`: **the local
  denominator lemma.** Around every point there is an affine open `V` and a nonzerodivisor
  `b ∈ Γ(X, V)` with `b · s` in the image of `L(V) ⟶ K_X(L)(V)`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_isAffineOpen_nhds_isNowhereDense_denominator`: the same, together
  with the nowhere density of the vanishing locus of `b` inside `V`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_nhds_forall_surjective_smul_of_isInvertible`: an invertible sheaf of
  modules on a scheme is generated by a single section near every point. This is the converse
  half of Tag 0B8M, restated in the spelling the ideal of denominators is written with.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_nhds_toSheafifyMeromorphicTensor_app_eq`: a meromorphic section is
  locally the class of a section of `K_X ⊗_{𝒪_X} L`.
* `Stacks.Meromorphic.exists_forall_smul_eval_eq_oneTmul`: the whole computation, done on an
  arbitrary site for an arbitrary morphism of sheaves of commutative rings.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.oneTmulMeromorphicSectionSheaf_app_apply`: the map `t ↦ 1 ⊗ t` and the
  unit of the change-of-rings adjunction agree on sections.

## Implementation notes

The mathematical content is three steps. Sheafification is locally surjective, so `s` is
locally the class of a section `z` of the presheaf `K_X ⊗_{𝒪_X} L`
(`CategoryTheory.Presheaf.imageSieve_mem`). Where `L` is generated by one section `a` — which
is the converse half of Tag 0B8M, available as
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.exists_nonempty_linearEquiv_of_isInvertible` — every element of
`K_X(V) ⊗_{𝒪_X(V)} L(V)` is a single pure tensor `u ⊗ a`. And `u` is locally a fraction `a'/b`
with `b` a nonzerodivisor, by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.exists_isAffineOpen_nhds_isFraction_totalQuotientSheaf`. Then
`b · s = 1 ⊗ a' • a` on that neighbourhood.

Two things force the shape of the file.

The map `L ⟶ K_X(L)` whose image the tag's ideal of denominators is defined by is the unit of
the change-of-rings adjunction, while the computation above naturally produces `t ↦ 1 ⊗ t`.
These are the same map on sections:
`Stacks.Sheaves.RingedToposModules.extendRestrictScalarsAdjunction_unit_app_val_app_apply` and
`Stacks.Sheaves.RingedToposModules.toExtendScalars_app_apply` both evaluate to
`toSheafify (1 ⊗ t)`, which is `AlgebraicGeometry.oneTmulMeromorphicSectionSheaf_app_apply`.

The module structures are spelled three incompatible ways on the same objects, and only some of
them are visible to instance search. `PresheafOfModules`' bridging instance for a base presheaf
of the form `R ⋙ forget₂ _ _` fires for `Stacks.PresheafOfModules.ChangeOfRings.ringPresheaf`,
which is an abbreviation of that shape, and does **not** fire for
`Stacks.Sheaves.Differentials.ringSheaf`, which is `sheafCompose` applied to `forget₂`. So no
statement in this file writes a scalar action of `Γ(X, V)` on `L(V)`: the generator condition
is written with the scalars in the `RingCat` spelling
`(Stacks.Sheaves.Differentials.ringSheaf X.sheaf).obj.obj (op V)`, where the plain `ModuleCat`
instance applies, and every tensor-product manipulation is done by a lemma stated on an
arbitrary site, where the spellings coincide. The same consideration splits the argument into
several small theorems: the elaborator spends a large part of the default heartbeat budget on
the defeq between the `Stacks.Sheaves.Differentials.ringSheaf` and `structureSheafRing`
spellings of `𝒪_X`, and each application of a scheme-level lemma pays it again.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 02P0](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02P0)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01X2](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01X2)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03CU](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03CU)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B8M](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B8M)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory Opposite TopologicalSpace TensorProduct
open Stacks.Sheaves.RingedToposModules
open scoped nonZeroDivisors

universe u

namespace Stacks.Meromorphic

/-- If every element of `M` is a scalar multiple `c • a` of one element `a`, then every element
of `S ⊗[R] M` is a pure tensor `u ⊗ₜ a`. -/
theorem exists_tmul_eq_of_surjective_smul {R : Type*} [CommRing R] {S : Type*} [CommRing S]
    [Algebra R S] {M : Type*} [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M] (a : M)
    (hsurj : Function.Surjective (fun c : R => c • a)) (z : TensorProduct R S M) :
    ∃ u : S, z = u ⊗ₜ[R] a := by
  induction z using TensorProduct.inductionOn with
  | tmul s m =>
    obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := hsurj m
    exact ⟨c • s, by rw [← hc]; exact (TensorProduct.smul_tmul _ _ _).symm⟩
  | add p q hp hq =>
    obtain ⟨u, hu⟩ := hp
    obtain ⟨w, hw⟩ := hq
    exact ⟨u + w, by rw [hu, hw, TensorProduct.add_tmul]⟩

/-- A module isomorphic to `R` is generated by the preimage of `1`: every element is a scalar
multiple of `e.symm 1`. -/
theorem surjective_smul_of_linearEquiv {R : Type*} [CommRing R] {M : Type*} [AddCommGroup M]
    [Module R M] (e : M ≃ₗ[R] R) : Function.Surjective (fun c : R => c • e.symm 1) := by
  intro m
  refine ⟨e m, ?_⟩
  change (e m) • e.symm 1 = m
  rw [← LinearEquiv.map_smul e.symm, smul_eq_mul, mul_one, e.symm_apply_apply]

/-- A scalar from `R` moves across the tensor product: `algebraMap R S c ⊗ₜ a = 1 ⊗ₜ (c • a)`. -/
theorem algebraMap_tmul_eq_one_tmul_smul {R : Type*} [CommRing R] {S : Type*} [CommRing S]
    [Algebra R S] {M : Type*} [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M] (c : R) (a : M) :
    (algebraMap R S c) ⊗ₜ[R] a = (1 : S) ⊗ₜ[R] (c • a) := by
  rw [TensorProduct.tmul_smul, TensorProduct.smul_tmul', Algebra.algebraMap_eq_smul_one]

/-- Clearing a denominator in a pure tensor: if `b a' : R` and `u : S` satisfy `u * b = a'` in
`S`, then multiplying `u ⊗ₜ a` by `b` gives `1 ⊗ₜ (a' • a)`. -/
theorem algebraMap_smul_tmul_eq_one_tmul_smul {R : Type*} [CommRing R] {S : Type*} [CommRing S]
    [Algebra R S] {M : Type*} [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M] (b a' : R) (u : S) (a : M)
    (heq : u * algebraMap R S b = algebraMap R S a') :
    (algebraMap R S b) • (u ⊗ₜ[R] a) = (1 : S) ⊗ₜ[R] (a' • a) := by
  rw [TensorProduct.smul_tmul', smul_eq_mul, mul_comm, heq, algebraMap_tmul_eq_one_tmul_smul]

section Site

variable {C : Type u} [SmallCategory C] (J : GrothendieckTopology C)
  {A₁ A₂ : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ CommRingCat.{u}} (θ : A₁ ⟶ A₂)
  (h₂ : Presheaf.IsSheaf J (Stacks.PresheafOfModules.ChangeOfRings.ringPresheaf A₂))
  [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [HasWeakSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{u}]

/-- The unit of sheafification at the presheaf extension of scalars `A₂ ⊗_{A₁} N`: the map
from the presheaf tensor product into the sheaf of modules it generates. -/
abbrev toSheafifyChangeOfRings (N : Stacks.PresheafOfModules.ChangeOfRings.PMod A₁) :=
  (PresheafOfModules.sheafificationAdjunction (R := commRingSheaf J A₂ h₂) (𝟙 _)).unit.app
    ((Stacks.PresheafOfModules.ChangeOfRings.changeOfRings θ).obj N)

/-- A section of the presheaf extension of scalars of `N` over an object on which `N` is
generated by a single element `a` is a pure tensor with second factor `a`. -/
theorem exists_tmul_eq_changeOfRings (N : Stacks.PresheafOfModules.ChangeOfRings.PMod A₁) (V : Cᵒᵖ)
  (a : N.obj V)
    (hsurj : Function.Surjective (fun c : (Stacks.PresheafOfModules.ChangeOfRings.ringPresheaf
      A₁).obj V => c • a))
    (z : ((Stacks.PresheafOfModules.ChangeOfRings.changeOfRings θ).obj N).obj V) :
    letI := (θ.app V).hom.toAlgebra
    ∃ u : A₂.obj V, z = u ⊗ₜ[A₁.obj V] a := by
  let := (θ.app V).hom.toAlgebra
  exact exists_tmul_eq_of_surjective_smul (R := A₁.obj V) a hsurj z

/-- Multiplying the class of `u ⊗ a` by the image of a section `b` whose product with `u` is
the image of `a'` gives the class of `1 ⊗ a' • a`, which is the image of `a' • a` under the
canonical map `N ⟶ (A₂ ⊗_{A₁} N)^#`. -/
theorem smul_toSheafifyChangeOfRings_tmul (N : Stacks.PresheafOfModules.ChangeOfRings.PMod A₁) (V :
  Cᵒᵖ)
    (b a' : A₁.obj V) (a : N.obj V) :
    letI := (θ.app V).hom.toAlgebra
    ∀ u : A₂.obj V, u * (θ.app V).hom b = (θ.app V).hom a' →
      ((θ.app V).hom b) •
          (((toSheafifyChangeOfRings J θ h₂ N).app V).hom (u ⊗ₜ[A₁.obj V] a))
        = ((toExtendScalars J θ h₂ N).app V).hom (a' • a) := by
  let alg := (θ.app V).hom.toAlgebra
  intro u heq
  have h1 : ((toSheafifyChangeOfRings J θ h₂ N).app V).hom
        ((((θ.app V).hom b) • (u ⊗ₜ[A₁.obj V] a) :
          ((Stacks.PresheafOfModules.ChangeOfRings.changeOfRings θ).obj N).obj V))
      = ((θ.app V).hom b) •
          (((toSheafifyChangeOfRings J θ h₂ N).app V).hom (u ⊗ₜ[A₁.obj V] a)) :=
    ((toSheafifyChangeOfRings J θ h₂ N).app V).hom.map_smul _ _
  have h2 : ((((θ.app V).hom b) • (u ⊗ₜ[A₁.obj V] a) :
        ((Stacks.PresheafOfModules.ChangeOfRings.changeOfRings θ).obj N).obj V))
      = (1 : A₂.obj V) ⊗ₜ[A₁.obj V] (a' • a) :=
    algebraMap_smul_tmul_eq_one_tmul_smul b a' u a heq
  rw [← h1, h2]
  exact (toExtendScalars_app_apply J θ h₂ N V (a' • a)).symm

/-- The form of `Stacks.Meromorphic.smul_toSheafifyChangeOfRings_tmul` that applies to the
restriction of a pure tensor along a morphism of the site. -/
theorem smul_toSheafifyChangeOfRings_map_tmul (N : Stacks.PresheafOfModules.ChangeOfRings.PMod A₁)
  {U V : Cᵒᵖ} (f : U ⟶ V)
    (b a' : A₁.obj V) :
    letI := (θ.app U).hom.toAlgebra
    ∀ (u : A₂.obj U) (a : N.obj U),
      (A₂.map f).hom u * (θ.app V).hom b = (θ.app V).hom a' →
      ((θ.app V).hom b) • (((toSheafifyChangeOfRings J θ h₂ N).app V).hom
          ((((Stacks.PresheafOfModules.ChangeOfRings.changeOfRings θ).obj N).map f).hom (u ⊗ₜ[A₁.obj
            U] a) :
            ((Stacks.PresheafOfModules.ChangeOfRings.changeOfRings θ).obj N).obj V))
        = ((toExtendScalars J θ h₂ N).app V).hom (a' • ((N.map f).hom a : N.obj V)) := by
  let algU := (θ.app U).hom.toAlgebra
  let algV := (θ.app V).hom.toAlgebra
  intro u a heq
  have hmap : ((((Stacks.PresheafOfModules.ChangeOfRings.changeOfRings θ).obj N).map f).hom
        (u ⊗ₜ[A₁.obj U] a) :
        ((Stacks.PresheafOfModules.ChangeOfRings.changeOfRings θ).obj N).obj V)
      = ((A₂.map f).hom u) ⊗ₜ[A₁.obj V] ((N.map f).hom a : N.obj V) :=
    Stacks.PresheafOfModules.ChangeOfRings.cofMap_tmul θ N f u a
  rw [hmap]
  exact smul_toSheafifyChangeOfRings_tmul J θ h₂ N V b a' _ _ heq

/-- The sheaf of modules generated by the presheaf extension of scalars `A₂ ⊗_{A₁} N`. -/
abbrev sheafifyChangeOfRings (N : Stacks.PresheafOfModules.ChangeOfRings.PMod A₁) :=
  (PresheafOfModules.sheafification (R := commRingSheaf J A₂ h₂) (𝟙 _)).obj
    ((Stacks.PresheafOfModules.ChangeOfRings.changeOfRings θ).obj N)

/-- A representative of a global section of `(A₂ ⊗_{A₁} N)^#` restricts to a representative. -/
theorem toSheafifyChangeOfRings_app_restrict_eq (N : Stacks.PresheafOfModules.ChangeOfRings.PMod A₁)
    (sM : (sheafifyChangeOfRings J θ h₂ N).sections) {U V : Cᵒᵖ} (f : U ⟶ V)
    (z : ((Stacks.PresheafOfModules.ChangeOfRings.changeOfRings θ).obj N).obj U)
    (hz : ((toSheafifyChangeOfRings J θ h₂ N).app U).hom z = sM.eval U) :
    ((toSheafifyChangeOfRings J θ h₂ N).app V).hom
        ((((Stacks.PresheafOfModules.ChangeOfRings.changeOfRings θ).obj N).map f).hom z :
          ((Stacks.PresheafOfModules.ChangeOfRings.changeOfRings θ).obj N).obj V)
      = sM.eval V := by
  refine (PresheafOfModules.naturality_apply (toSheafifyChangeOfRings J θ h₂ N) f z).trans ?_
  rw [hz]
  exact PresheafOfModules.sections_property sM f

/-- **The denominator identity, in the form that only needs a local representative and a local
generator.** If a global section `sM` of `(A₂ ⊗_{A₁} N)^#` is the class of `z` over `U`, and `N`
is generated over `U` by `a`, then there is `u : A₂(U)` such that over every further object `V`
and every pair `b, a'` with `u|_V · θ(b) = θ(a')`, multiplying `sM` by `θ(b)` gives the class of
`1 ⊗ a' • a|_V`. -/
theorem exists_forall_smul_eval_eq_oneTmul (N : Stacks.PresheafOfModules.ChangeOfRings.PMod A₁) {U :
  Cᵒᵖ} (a : N.obj U)
    (hsurj : Function.Surjective (fun c : (Stacks.PresheafOfModules.ChangeOfRings.ringPresheaf
      A₁).obj U => c • a))
    (z : ((Stacks.PresheafOfModules.ChangeOfRings.changeOfRings θ).obj N).obj U)
    (sM : (sheafifyChangeOfRings J θ h₂ N).sections)
    (hz : ((toSheafifyChangeOfRings J θ h₂ N).app U).hom z = sM.eval U) :
    ∃ u : A₂.obj U, ∀ (V : Cᵒᵖ) (f : U ⟶ V) (b a' : A₁.obj V),
      (A₂.map f).hom u * (θ.app V).hom b = (θ.app V).hom a' →
      ((θ.app V).hom b) • sM.eval V
        = ((toExtendScalars J θ h₂ N).app V).hom (a' • ((N.map f).hom a : N.obj V)) := by
  obtain ⟨u, hu⟩ := exists_tmul_eq_changeOfRings θ N U a hsurj z
  refine ⟨u, fun V f b a' heq => ?_⟩
  have hsV := toSheafifyChangeOfRings_app_restrict_eq J θ h₂ N sM f z hz
  rw [hu] at hsV
  rw [← hsV]
  exact smul_toSheafifyChangeOfRings_map_tmul J θ h₂ N f b a' u a heq

/-- The morphism of sheaves of modules out of the structure sheaf determined by a global
section acts on sections by scalar multiplication. -/
theorem unitHomEquiv_symm_val_app_apply {J' : GrothendieckTopology C} (R : Sheaf J' RingCat.{u})
    (M : SheafOfModules.{u} R) (s : M.sections) (V : Cᵒᵖ) (r : R.obj.obj V) :
    ((M.unitHomEquiv.symm s).val.app V).hom r = r • s.eval V := rfl

end Site

end Stacks.Meromorphic

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

variable (X : Scheme.{u})
  (L : SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.Sheaves.Differentials.ringSheaf (J := Opens.grothendieckTopology
    X) X.sheaf))

/-- The presheaf `K_X ⊗_{𝒪_X} L` of which `K_X(L)` is the sheafification. -/
abbrev meromorphicTensorPresheaf :=
  (Stacks.PresheafOfModules.ChangeOfRings.changeOfRings X.toTotalQuotientSheaf.hom).obj L.val

/-- The canonical map from `K_X ⊗_{𝒪_X} L` to its sheafification `K_X(L)`. -/
abbrev toSheafifyMeromorphicTensor :=
  Stacks.Meromorphic.toSheafifyChangeOfRings (Opens.grothendieckTopology X)
    X.toTotalQuotientSheaf.hom
    (Stacks.Sheaves.Differentials.ringSheaf (J := Opens.grothendieckTopology X)
      X.totalQuotientSheaf).property L.val

/-- The map `t ↦ 1 ⊗ t` from `L` into `K_X(L)`. It agrees on sections with the unit
`AlgebraicGeometry.toMeromorphicSectionSheafAsModule`, by
`AlgebraicGeometry.oneTmulMeromorphicSectionSheaf_app_apply`. -/
abbrev oneTmulMeromorphicSectionSheaf :=
  Stacks.Sheaves.RingedToposModules.toExtendScalars (Opens.grothendieckTopology X)
    X.toTotalQuotientSheaf.hom
    (Stacks.Sheaves.Differentials.ringSheaf (J := Opens.grothendieckTopology X)
      X.totalQuotientSheaf).property
    L.val

/-- **The map `t ↦ 1 ⊗ t` is the unit of extension of scalars, on sections.** Both
`AlgebraicGeometry.oneTmulMeromorphicSectionSheaf` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.toMeromorphicSectionSheafAsModule` send a section `t` of `L` over `V` to the
image of `1 ⊗ t` under the map to the sheafification, so they agree. -/
theorem oneTmulMeromorphicSectionSheaf_app_apply (V : (Opens X)ᵒᵖ) (t : L.val.obj V) :
    ((oneTmulMeromorphicSectionSheaf X L).app V).hom t
      = ((toMeromorphicSectionSheafAsModule X L).val.app V).hom t := by
  rw [toMeromorphicSectionSheafAsModule_val_app_apply]
  exact Stacks.Sheaves.RingedToposModules.toExtendScalars_app_apply
    (Opens.grothendieckTopology X) X.toTotalQuotientSheaf.hom
    (Stacks.Sheaves.Differentials.ringSheaf (J := Opens.grothendieckTopology X)
      X.totalQuotientSheaf).property
    L.val V t

/-- **An invertible sheaf of modules on a scheme is generated by one section near every point.**
Around every point there is an open set on each open subset of which `L` has a single
generator. This is the converse half of Tag 0B8M, read in the spelling the ideal of
denominators is stated with. -/
theorem exists_nhds_forall_surjective_smul_of_isInvertible
    (hL : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.sheaf.obj
      (Stacks.Sheaves.Differentials.ringSheaf (J := Opens.grothendieckTopology X) X.sheaf).property
        L) (x : X) :
    ∃ W : X.Opens, x ∈ W ∧ ∀ V : X.Opens, V ≤ W → ∃ a : L.val.obj (op V),
      Function.Surjective (fun c : (Stacks.Sheaves.Differentials.ringSheaf
        (J := Opens.grothendieckTopology X) X.sheaf).obj.obj (op V) => c • a) := by
  have hloc : ∀ y : X.toRingedSpace.carrier,
      IsLocalRing (Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorStalkRingedSpace.ringStalk X.toRingedSpace y) :=
    fun y => X.isLocalRing y
  have hinv : Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.toRingedSpace.presheaf
      (structureSheafRing X.toRingedSpace).property L :=
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.isInvertible_iff_algebraicGeometry _ _ L).mpr hL
  obtain ⟨W, hxW, hW⟩ := Stacks.SheafOfModules.exists_nonempty_linearEquiv_of_isInvertible
    (X := X.toRingedSpace) L x
  refine ⟨W, hxW, fun V hVW => ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨e⟩ := hW V hVW
  exact ⟨e.symm 1, Stacks.Meromorphic.surjective_smul_of_linearEquiv e⟩

/-- **A meromorphic section of `L` is, near every point, the class of a section of
`K_X ⊗_{𝒪_X} L`.** This is local surjectivity of sheafification; there is in general no such
section over all of `X`, because `K_X` is a sheafification and not the presheaf of fractions. -/
theorem exists_nhds_toSheafifyMeromorphicTensor_app_eq
    (s : MeromorphicSection X.sheaf L) (x : X) :
    ∃ W : X.Opens, x ∈ W ∧ ∃ z : (meromorphicTensorPresheaf X L).obj (op W),
      ((toSheafifyMeromorphicTensor X L).app (op W)).hom z = s.eval (op W) := by
  have hLS : Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective (Opens.grothendieckTopology X)
      ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf _).map (toSheafifyMeromorphicTensor X L)) := by
    change Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective (Opens.grothendieckTopology X)
      (CategoryTheory.toSheafify (Opens.grothendieckTopology X)
        (meromorphicTensorPresheaf X L).presheaf)
    infer_instance
  have hls := CategoryTheory.Presheaf.imageSieve_mem (Opens.grothendieckTopology X)
    ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf _).map (toSheafifyMeromorphicTensor X L))
    (U := op (⊤ : X.Opens)) (s.eval (op (⊤ : X.Opens)))
  rw [Opens.mem_grothendieckTopology] at hls
  obtain ⟨W, f, ⟨zz, hzz⟩, hxW⟩ := hls x (Opens.mem_top x)
  exact ⟨W, hxW, zz, hzz.trans (PresheafOfModules.sections_property s f.op)⟩

/-- A representative of a meromorphic section restricts to a representative. -/
theorem toSheafifyMeromorphicTensor_app_restrict_eq
    (s : MeromorphicSection X.sheaf L) {W W' : X.Opens} (hle : W' ≤ W)
    (z : (meromorphicTensorPresheaf X L).obj (op W))
    (hz : ((toSheafifyMeromorphicTensor X L).app (op W)).hom z = s.eval (op W)) :
    ((toSheafifyMeromorphicTensor X L).app (op W')).hom
        (((meromorphicTensorPresheaf X L).map (homOfLE hle).op).hom z :
          (meromorphicTensorPresheaf X L).obj (op W'))
      = s.eval (op W') := by
  exact Stacks.Meromorphic.toSheafifyChangeOfRings_app_restrict_eq _ _ _ L.val s
    (homOfLE hle).op z hz

/-- The two local inputs the denominator argument needs, found on one neighbourhood: a
representative of `s` in `K_X ⊗_{𝒪_X} L`, and a single generator of `L`. -/
theorem exists_nhds_representative_and_generator
    (hL : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.sheaf.obj
      (Stacks.Sheaves.Differentials.ringSheaf (J := Opens.grothendieckTopology X) X.sheaf).property
        L)
    (s : MeromorphicSection X.sheaf L) (x : X) :
    ∃ W : X.Opens, x ∈ W ∧
      (∃ a : L.val.obj (op W), Function.Surjective (fun c : (Stacks.Sheaves.Differentials.ringSheaf
        (J := Opens.grothendieckTopology X) X.sheaf).obj.obj (op W) => c • a)) ∧
      ∃ z : (meromorphicTensorPresheaf X L).obj (op W),
        ((toSheafifyMeromorphicTensor X L).app (op W)).hom z = s.eval (op W) := by
  obtain ⟨W, hxW, z, hz⟩ := exists_nhds_toSheafifyMeromorphicTensor_app_eq X L s x
  obtain ⟨W₀, hxW₀, hW₀⟩ := exists_nhds_forall_surjective_smul_of_isInvertible X L hL x
  obtain ⟨W₁, hW₁W, hW₁W₀, hxW₁⟩ : ∃ W₁ : X.Opens, W₁ ≤ W ∧ W₁ ≤ W₀ ∧ x ∈ W₁ :=
    ⟨W ⊓ W₀, inf_le_left, inf_le_right, ⟨hxW, hxW₀⟩⟩
  exact ⟨W₁, hxW₁, hW₀ W₁ hW₁W₀,
    _, toSheafifyMeromorphicTensor_app_restrict_eq X L s hW₁W z hz⟩

/-- **A meromorphic section of an invertible sheaf has a nonzerodivisor denominator on an
affine neighbourhood of every point**, for the map `t ↦ 1 ⊗ t` into `K_X(L)`. -/
theorem exists_isAffineOpen_nhds_oneTmul_eq
    (hL : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.sheaf.obj
      (Stacks.Sheaves.Differentials.ringSheaf (J := Opens.grothendieckTopology X) X.sheaf).property
        L)
    (s : MeromorphicSection X.sheaf L) (x : X) :
    ∃ V : X.Opens, x ∈ V ∧ IsAffineOpen V ∧ ∃ b ∈ (Γ(X, V))⁰, ∃ t : L.val.obj (op V),
      ((meromorphicSectionMul X L s).val.app (op V)).hom b
        = ((oneTmulMeromorphicSectionSheaf X L).app (op V)).hom t := by
  obtain ⟨W, hxW, ⟨a, hsurj⟩, z, hz⟩ := exists_nhds_representative_and_generator X L hL s x
  obtain ⟨u, hgen⟩ := Stacks.Meromorphic.exists_forall_smul_eval_eq_oneTmul
    (Opens.grothendieckTopology X) X.toTotalQuotientSheaf.hom
    (Stacks.Sheaves.Differentials.ringSheaf (J := Opens.grothendieckTopology X)
      X.totalQuotientSheaf).property
    L.val a hsurj z s hz
  obtain ⟨V, hVW, hVaff, hxV, a', b, hb, hbu, heq⟩ :=
    X.exists_isAffineOpen_nhds_isFraction_totalQuotientSheaf (U := W) u hxW
  exact ⟨V, hxV, hVaff, b, hb, _, ((meromorphicSectionMul_val_app X L s (op V) b).trans
    (Stacks.Meromorphic.unitHomEquiv_symm_val_app_apply _ _ s (op V) _)).trans
      (hgen (op V) (homOfLE hVW).op b a' heq)⟩

/-- **The local denominator lemma for Stacks Tag 02P0.** For an invertible sheaf of modules `L`
on a scheme and a meromorphic section `s` of `L`, every point has an *affine* open
neighbourhood `V` on which some nonzerodivisor `b ∈ Γ(X, V)` is a denominator of `s`: the
product `b · s` is the image of a section of `L` over `V`. Equivalently, `b` lies in the ideal
of denominators of `s` over `V`.

This is the local form of the reduction the source makes when it writes `s = a/b` with `b` a
nonzerodivisor after shrinking `X` and trivializing `L`. It is stated locally on purpose: the
sheaf of total quotient rings is a *sheafification*, so there is in general no global fraction,
and the corresponding global statement is false. -/
theorem exists_isAffineOpen_nhds_toMeromorphicSectionSheafAsModule_eq
    (hL : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.sheaf.obj
      (Stacks.Sheaves.Differentials.ringSheaf (J := Opens.grothendieckTopology X) X.sheaf).property
        L)
    (s : MeromorphicSection X.sheaf L) (x : X) :
    ∃ V : X.Opens, x ∈ V ∧ IsAffineOpen V ∧ ∃ b ∈ (Γ(X, V))⁰, ∃ t : L.val.obj (op V),
      ((meromorphicSectionMul X L s).val.app (op V)).hom b
        = ((toMeromorphicSectionSheafAsModule X L).val.app (op V)).hom t := by
  obtain ⟨V, hxV, hVaff, b, hb, t, ht⟩ := exists_isAffineOpen_nhds_oneTmul_eq X L hL s x
  exact ⟨V, hxV, hVaff, b, hb, t,
    ht.trans (oneTmulMeromorphicSectionSheaf_app_apply X L (op V) t)⟩

/-- **The local denominator lemma packaged with its topological consequence.** On the affine
neighbourhood produced by
`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_isAffineOpen_nhds_toMeromorphicSectionSheafAsModule_eq`, the locus
where the denominator `b` vanishes is nowhere dense in `X`. Since `b` lies in the ideal of
denominators of `s` over `V`, the vanishing locus of that ideal inside `V` is contained in this
nowhere dense set; this is the step the source records as "it is clear that `(b) ⊆ I`, hence
`V(I) ⊆ V(b)` is nowhere dense". -/
theorem exists_isAffineOpen_nhds_isNowhereDense_denominator
    (hL : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.sheaf.obj
      (Stacks.Sheaves.Differentials.ringSheaf (J := Opens.grothendieckTopology X) X.sheaf).property
        L)
    (s : MeromorphicSection X.sheaf L) (x : X) :
    ∃ V : X.Opens, x ∈ V ∧ IsAffineOpen V ∧ ∃ b ∈ (Γ(X, V))⁰,
      IsNowhereDense ((V : Set X) \ (X.basicOpen b : Set X)) ∧
      ∃ t : L.val.obj (op V),
        ((meromorphicSectionMul X L s).val.app (op V)).hom b
          = ((toMeromorphicSectionSheafAsModule X L).val.app (op V)).hom t := by
  obtain ⟨V, hxV, hVaff, b, hb, t, ht⟩ :=
    exists_isAffineOpen_nhds_toMeromorphicSectionSheafAsModule_eq X L hL s x
  exact ⟨V, hxV, hVaff, b, hb,
    isNowhereDense_sdiff_basicOpen_of_mem_nonZeroDivisors hVaff hb, t, ht⟩

end AlgebraicGeometry
